notes:
Dedicated dataflow machine, not the LM-1 ISA. Bit-parallel BFS run backwards from
the flag, so each robot move is a local decision and the up/right/down/left
tie-break falls out of neighbour order — no path storage. Distance mod 3 (the grid
is bipartite) in three label planes whose roles rotate for free: pushing them back
into the ring in a different order *is* the rotation. free = NB | S1 | S2 | S3, so
no fifth plane. g = 255 - p (a 180 deg rotation) keeps every plane word
non-negative, which makes bit tests branch-free. 51 blocks over one man, an
18-word ring, a spill FIFO and a scratch FIFO.

Server ticks ran 1.31x the local figure (362,323 vs 277,368).
Beat the previous board leader (1.2e10).
